{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793197174,"nonce":"eDVoApNNrsoa9pFl9X61zcuI+nU=","message":"Picked up implementation on main. Current work adds lossless AIR persistence for native and WASM AOT, with target/ABI/profile/compiler identity, whole-module metadata invalidation and recorded per-function callee dependencies. Storage uses checksummed entries, verification, atomic publication, a process lock and bounded LRU eviction; the in-memory AIR retention policy remains separate. Adding CLI inspection/clear/disable/budget controls and cross-process behavior tests.\n\nAlso investigating the reported slow WASM builds by timing decode/preparation, AIR lowering/passes, LLVM IR emission, LLVM middle-end/codegen and linking separately. Initial Ashui WindowPage logs show 3,222 bytecode functions producing 8,150 LLVM bodies plus 1,164 call trampolines; most shards carry about 6,000 small functions for inlining. Measurements under concurrent Rust compilation are preliminary; controlled cold/warm/edit runs will follow after validation.","files":null}]}